                <pb facs="0503" n="433" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg433"/>

                <head>No. 229.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lowell to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-05-29"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 29, 1883</date>.
                        (Received June 9.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 557.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acquaint you that on
                    the 21st instant I received your No. 586 of the 5th instant, and immediately
                    placed it in the hands of the copyist. I was not able to make an appointment to
                    communicate it to Lord Granville for an earlier date than to-day. I have just
                    now returned from the foreign office, where I had an interview with his
                    lordship, and read this instruction to him, agreeably to your direction. I also
                    left a copy of it with him at his desire.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>J. R. LOWELL.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
